<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell"><h2 id=3D"HighLevelDesignDocumentContactCenterBAUR=
12.0-PurposeofHLD">Purpose of HLD<span class=3D"copy-heading-link-container=
"><button class=3D"copy-heading-link-button" aria-label=3D"Copy link to hea=
ding" data-heading-id=3D"HighLevelDesignDocumentContactCenterBAUR12.0-Purpo=
seofHLD"><span class=3D"aui-icon aui-iconfont-link copy-heading-link-img" r=
ole=3D"img" aria-label=3D"Copy link to heading"></span><span class=3D"aui-i=
con aui-iconfont-approve copy-heading-link-img" role=3D"img" aria-label=3D"=
Copied!"></span><span class=3D"aui-icon aui-iconfont-cross-circle copy-head=
ing-link-img" role=3D"img" aria-label=3D"Error copying link"></span></butto=
n></span></h2><p>The High Level Design Document (HLD) is the single solutio=
n document created during a project. It contains solution summary, architec=
tural information and solution details that are used as an input for develo=
pment and testing activities.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell"><h2 id=3D"HighLevelDesignDocumentContactCenterBAUR=
12.0-HowtoCompletethisDocument">How to Complete this Document<span class=3D=
"copy-heading-link-container"><button class=3D"copy-heading-link-button" ar=
ia-label=3D"Copy link to heading" data-heading-id=3D"HighLevelDesignDocumen=
tContactCenterBAUR12.0-HowtoCompletethisDocument"><span class=3D"aui-icon a=
ui-iconfont-link copy-heading-link-img" role=3D"img" aria-label=3D"Copy lin=
k to heading"></span><span class=3D"aui-icon aui-iconfont-approve copy-head=
ing-link-img" role=3D"img" aria-label=3D"Copied!"></span><span class=3D"aui=
-icon aui-iconfont-cross-circle copy-heading-link-img" role=3D"img" aria-la=
bel=3D"Error copying link"></span></button></span></h2><ul><li>The BSA (or =
Solution Delivery Manager in the case where the project is without a BSA) i=
s responsible for collating information and populating Business Section (Se=
ction 1) of this document</li><li>The Solution Architect (SA), with input f=
rom the Infra Solution Architect, ICSU and the Enterprise Architect is resp=
onsible for completing the Architecture Section (Section 2) of this documen=
t</li><li>After the completion of Sections 1 and 2, the SA is responsible f=
or submitting the HLD to the DA for approval</li><li>Sequel to DA approval,=
 the BSA (Solution Delivery Manager in the case where the project is withou=
t a BSA) is responsible for coordinating and consolidating inputs from requ=
isite Tech teams to complete the Technical Section (Section 3) of this docu=
ment and obtaining sign-offs as required.</li><li>This document must be sub=
mitted technical and business stakeholder approvals via Jira workflow, leve=
raging a Jira HLD ticket (see <a href=3D"https://reqcentral.com/wiki/displa=
y/JPP2T/How+to+Create+an+HLD+Artifact+ticket" rel=3D"nofollow">How to Creat=
e an HLD Artifact ticket</a> for details).</li><li>It is recommended that t=
his document (HLD) be hosted as a shared document on the Project website so=
 updates can be made simultaneously by participating stakeholders</li></ul>=
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"columnLayout two-equal" data-layout=3D"two-equal">
